 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The golden rule of the negative «tu» imperative",
     "texto": [
      "To tell an informal listener NOT to do something, Italian always uses the fixed structure: **non + verb in the infinitive**: **Non parlare!** (don't speak!), **Non aprire la porta!** (don't open the door!), **Non dimenticare il biglietto!** (don't forget the ticket!).",
      "One never says *non parli* or *non parla* to forbid something to «tu»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Placement of pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "In the informal negative imperative, pronouns can go before the infinitive or attached to its ending: **Non farlo!** = **Non lo fare!**; **Non ti preoccupare!** = **Non preoccuparti!**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Affirmative versus negative imperative (tu)",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Affirmative (do it!)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Negative (don't do it!)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Grammar rule",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
